{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Test contract card (frozen before implementation)\n\nBehavior under test: `rebar fsck --repair --only=stale-channel` selects only tickets whose latest active snapshot lacks `compiled_state.creation_channel` while a retained CREATE exists, and runs them through the existing pre-tagged, batched, commit-and-push repair engine.\n\nSafety invariants: refuse a selected ticket when it also has SNAPSHOT_INCONSISTENT or ORPHAN_EVENT; do not mutate unrelated A3 faults; preserve legacy `--repair` and broad `--repair-snapshots`; reject unknown `--only` and `--only` without `--repair` with exit 2; dry-run writes nothing; `--limit` remains resumable; push failure aborts.\n\nHappy-path tests shown to implementer: plan detects stale channel, stale-only dry-run selects it, stale-only live rebuild clears it.\nHeld-out tests: mixed-fault refusal, parser misuse/unknown values, default repair behavior, limit/resumption, push failure, real-git batching and rollback rehearsal.\nOracle: fsck finding tags before/after, exact repair-plan buckets and report lines, git tree/commit/ref comparisons, and full existing test suite. Edge tests are physically withheld from the implementation worktree during the implementation attempt."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785870825249820001,"uuid":"7206e800-6f80-4dbf-a22a-e0df2f5bc06b"}